1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,559
So the first tip is around what you should be spending your time on.
第一个建议，涉及你应该把时间花在哪些地方。

2
00:00:03,559 --> 00:00:07,080
Now four days is probably the max amount of time that you'll stay here.
作者觉得，来这里大概最多会待四天。

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:13,150
So if you only have one or two days in the cotswolds these are the places I would put at the top of the list.
所以，如果你在科茨沃尔德只有一两天，我会把下面这些地方放在优先清单上。

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:20,679
If you have one day I think bourton on the water bibury and lower and upper slaughter are perfect since they are all in close proximity.
如果只有一天，作者认为水上伯顿、Bibury，以及 Lower Slaughter 和 Upper Slaughter 很合适，因为它们彼此距离近。

5
00:00:20,679 --> 00:00:25,160
Broadway and castle combe were both great but are very north and very south.
Broadway 和 Castle Combe 都很棒，不过一个很靠北，一个很靠南，

6
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:29,710
So it really depends on what else you're doing and where else you want to go that's near.
所以要看你还准备做什么，以及附近还想去哪儿。

7
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:36,840
From a managing expectations point of view lots of these places are simply villages and not much else is going on beyond that.
从管理期待的角度说，很多地方就是村庄而已，除此之外没有太多别的活动。

8
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:42,760
Castle combe for example was lovely but was basically just a stretch of houses and could be done in 30 minutes.
比如 Castle Combe 很漂亮，但基本就是一段房屋，作者觉得三十分钟就能逛完。

9
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:49,150
So do bear that in mind if you're planning on driving an hour just to get to one destination.
因此，如果打算开一小时车只去一个地方，记得考虑这一点。

10
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:53,920
For places such as bourton and the slaughters get there as early as possible.
作者建议，去水上伯顿和 Slaughter 两村这样的地方，尽可能早点到。

11
00:00:54,200 --> 00:01:00,349
We arrived at 9 am and found a parking spot fairly easily but it was full one hour later.
我们早上九点到，很容易就找到了停车位，但一小时后就停满了。

12
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:08,109
For lower slaughter I actually don't think there's any real parking to speak of so we just found some country road and then walked back.
至于 Lower Slaughter，作者觉得几乎没什么停车设施可说，所以我们找了条乡间小路停车，再走回来。

13
00:01:08,119 --> 00:01:18,190
We found that entering the term free parking when searching on google maps did just that so try that term instead of just parking.
我们发现，在 Google 地图上搜索“免费停车”，确实能找到相应结果，所以作者建议试试这个词，而不只是搜“停车”。

14
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:26,190
When we planned our route I basically just looked at loads of blogs and vlogs such as this one and added places of interest to my map.
规划路线时，我基本上看了很多博客和像这部这样的旅行视频，然后把感兴趣的地点加到我的地图上。

15
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:34,030
That was ultimately why we booked the airbnb that we did because it was literally right in the middle of everywhere that we wanted to go.
这也是我们最终订那家 Airbnb 的原因，因为它恰好位于所有想去地点的中间。

16
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:44,190
The room was 136 pounds per night with breakfast included and for us was perfect to be in the middle of nowhere where it was silent and peaceful.
作者当时订的房间每晚一百三十六英镑，含早餐。对我们来说，住在这样安静祥和、远离人烟的地方，正合心意。

17
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:49,080
I've stayed within bourton on the water before which has the benefit of feeling like it's your own village.
我以前也住过水上伯顿，优点是会感觉整座村庄都像是自己的一样，

18
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:56,000
Where you can take a walk for dinner or breakfast but it obviously wasn't as much of the country escape as we had this time around.
可以步行出去吃晚餐或早餐，但显然没有我们这次这样强烈的乡村逃离感。

19
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:04,840
One thing I didn't cover from the main vlog mostly for the modern day trend of eating your food in the dark is gastropubs.
正片里有一件事我没讲到，那就是美食酒吧，主要是因为如今流行在昏暗环境里吃饭。

20
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:13,950
They are everywhere in the cotswolds and often the only type of restaurant around visit them visit often they are awesome.
科茨沃尔德到处都有美食酒吧，而且常常是附近唯一一类餐厅；作者很喜欢，推荐大家常去。

21
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,119
I'm not sure if this was a one off for us.
我不确定这是否只是我们碰到的偶然情况，

22
00:02:16,119 --> 00:02:22,349
But if you're traveling during peak season I'd advise on making reservations at restaurants before you travel there.
但如果你在旺季旅行，作者会建议出发前先预订餐厅，

23
00:02:22,359 --> 00:02:33,150
Especially if you need to take a drive just to get there when we called ahead to places in cirencester for example it took four different phone calls until we found somewhere with space.
尤其是需要专门开车过去时；比如我们提前打电话问 Cirencester 的餐厅，打到第四家才找到有空位的。

24
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:39,229
Making a reservation a few hours before should be enough but just something to keep in mind.
作者觉得提前几小时订应该就够了，只是想提醒大家留意这一点。

25
00:02:39,239 --> 00:02:47,200
As I quickly mentioned during the vlog all cafes and shops seem to close at 5 pm with the exception of restaurants and pubs.
正如正片里简短提过的，作者当时觉得，除了餐厅和酒吧外，咖啡馆和商店似乎下午五点就都关了。

26
00:02:47,559 --> 00:02:58,109
I'm not sure if that's a country thing or a pandemic thing but yeah chipping campden seemed like a lovely town but with everything shut the visit lost some of its charm and energy.
我不确定那是乡村习惯还是疫情时期的情况；Chipping Campden 看上去很可爱，但店都关了，就少了一些魅力与活力。

27
00:02:58,119 --> 00:03:03,310
For transport we took a 55 minute direct train from marylebone to banbury station.
交通方面，我们当时从 Marylebone 坐了五十五分钟直达火车到 Banbury 站，

28
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:07,680
Which is the quickest way to get to the edge of the cotswolds at least from london.
作者认为，这至少是从伦敦到科茨沃尔德边缘最快的方式。

29
00:03:08,039 --> 00:03:13,320
There is then an enterprise car rental just outside the station and we drove from there.
车站外当时就有 Enterprise 租车点，我们从那里取车开走。

30
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:17,720
I'm still not sure if that's a normal way to do it rather than just rent a car from london.
我仍不确定大家通常是不是这样做，还是会直接在伦敦租车。

31
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:25,080
But since we live on the east side it means we have to drive through the city or around the m 25 both of which can be a nightmare.
但我们住在东边，如果从伦敦开车，就得穿过市区或绕 M25，这两种方式都可能很折腾。

32
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:30,600
This basically meant that we only had to drive around the quieter country roads which suited us fine.
这样我们基本只需要在比较安静的乡间道路上开车，正合我们的心意。

33
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:35,280
The car was 150 pounds for four days and 35 pounds for petrol.
作者当时租车四天花了一百五十英镑，汽油花了三十五英镑。

34
00:03:35,639 --> 00:03:38,680
The return train journey was 33 pounds per person.
往返火车票当时是每人三十三英镑。

35
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:44,759
But remember it's always best to book in advance for trains in the uk 12 weeks is usually the sweet spot.
不过，作者提醒，在英国坐火车最好提前订票；他觉得提前十二周通常是比较理想的时点，

36
00:03:44,759 --> 00:03:49,920
But maybe do a cost comparison from wherever you're coming from and see what's best.
但还是可以根据自己的出发地比较一下费用，看看哪种方式最合适。
